    40	# Dataset Description
    41	The dataset of the artifact exists in the `data/` directory and has the following structure:
    42	```
    43	├── data
    44	│   ├── results
    45	│   │   ├── rq1a.csv
    46	│   │   ├── rq1b.csv
    47	│   │   ├── rq2a.csv
    48	│   │   └── rq2b.csv
    49	│   │   ├── qualitative_results.json
    50	│   ├── project_dependencies_post_data_collection.json
    51	│   ├── project_dependencies_final.json
    52	│   ├── security
    53	│   │   ├── project_vulnerabilities.json
    54	│   │   ├── pypi_vulnerabilities.csv
    55	│   │   ├── vulnerability2function.json
    56	│   │   └── vulnerable_dependencies.json
    57	│   └── subset
    58	│       ├── sample_projects.csv
    59	```
    60	Bellow, we describe the contents of each file:
    61	
    62	- `results/`: This directory stores the bre-baked dataset of the automated and manual analysis performed in order to produce the results (numbers, figures, tables) reported on the results section of our paper (Sections 3.1-3.4)
    63	  - `rq1a.csv`: Contains the quantitative analysis results for the first research question (RQ1), focusing especially on the prevalence of bloat at different granularities in the Python projects.
    64	    - Columns:
    65	      - `project`: GitHub Owner-Repository Name.
    66	      - `NBD`: Number of Bloated Dependencies – Represents the number of bloated dependencies identified in the project.
    67	      - `NBFD`: Number of Bloated Files in Dependencies – Measures the count of bloated files identified within the dependencies of the project.
    68	      - `NBMD`: Number of Bloated Methods in Dependencies – Indicates the count of bloated methods found within the dependencies of the project.
    69	      - `NBD-LOC`: Number of Bloated Dependencies in LOC - Denotes the lines of code (LOC) in the bloated dependencies.
    70	      - `NBFD-LOC`: Number of Bloated Files in Dependencies in LOC - Represents the lines of code (LOC) in the bloated files of the dependencies.
    71	      - `NBMD-LOC`: Number of Bloated Methods in Dependencies in LOC - Represents the number of lines of code (LOC) in the bloated methods of the dependencies.
    72	      - `PBD`: Percentage of Bloated Dependencies – Represents the proportion of dependencies that are identified as bloated in the project.
    73	      - `PBFD`: Percentage of Bloated Files in Dependencies – Represents the proportion of files within the dependencies that are identified as bloated.
    74	      - `PBMD`: Percentage of Bloated Methods in Dependencies – Represents the proportion of methods within the dependencies of the project that are identified as bloated.
    75	      - `PBD-LOC`: Percentage of Bloated Dependencies in LOC - Represents the percentage of lines of code (LOC) in dependencies that are bloated
    76	      - `PBFD-LOC`: Percentage of Bloated Files in Dependencies in LOC - Represents the percentage of lines of code (LOC) in dependency files that are bloated.
    77	      - `PBMD-LOC`: Percentage of Bloated Methods in Dependencies in LOC - Represents the percentage of lines of code (LOC) in dependency methods that are bloated.
    78	      - `unique_unresolved_count`: The number of unique unresolved external calls during the Stitching process.
    79	      - `unique_resolved_count`: The number of unique resolved external calls during the Stitching process.
    80	      - `unresolved_count`: The total number of unresolved external calls during the Stitching process.
    81	      - `resolved_count`: The total number of resolved external calls during the Stitching process.
    82	
    83	- `rq1b.csv`: For each Python project, this file includes the different usage statuses of its direct and transitive dependencies, showcasing metrics related to bloat and usage in various granularities (RQ1).
    84	  - Columns:
    85	    - `product`: GitHub Owner-Repository Name.
    86	    - `bloated_deps_count_1`: Number of bloated direct dependencies.
    87	    - `bloated_deps_loc_1`: Lines of code in bloated direct dependencies.
    88	    - `bloated_files_count_1`: Number of bloated files in direct dependencies.
    89	    - `bloated_files_loc_1`: Lines of code in the bloated files of direct dependencies.
    90	    - `bloated_functions_count_1`: Number of bloated functions in direct dependencies.
    91	    - `bloated_functions_loc_1`: Total number of lines of code in the bloated functions of direct dependencies.
    92	    - `used_direct_deps_count_1`: Number of used direct dependencies.
    93	    - `used_direct_deps_count_1`: Lines of code in used direct dependencies.
    94	    - `used_direct_files_count_1`: Number of used files in direct dependencies.
    95	    - `used_direct_files_loc_1`: Lines of code in the used files of direct dependencies.
    96	    - `used_direct_functions_count_1`: Number of used functions in direct dependencies.
    97	    - `used_direct_functions_loc_1`: Lines of code in the used functions of direct dependencies.
    98	    - `transitive_bloated_dependencies_count`: Number of bloated transitive dependencies.
    99	    - `transitive_bloated_dependencies_loc`: Lines of code in bloated transitive dependencies.
   100	    - `transitive_bloated_files_count`: Number of bloated files in transitive dependencies.
   101	    - `transitive_bloated_files_loc`: Lines of code in the bloated files of transitive dependencies.
   102	    - `transitive_bloated_functions_count`: Number of bloated functions in transitive dependencies.
   103	    - `transitive_bloated_functions_loc`: Lines of code in the bloated functions of transitive dependencies.
   104	    - `transitive_used_dependencies_count`: Number of used transitive dependencies.
   105	    - `transitive_used_dependencies_loc`: Lines of code in used transitive dependencies.
   106	    - `transitive_used_files_count`: Number of used files in transitive dependencies.
   107	    - `transitive_used_files_loc`: Lines of code in the used files of transitive dependencies.
   108	    - `transitive_used_functions_count`: Number of used functions in transitive dependencies.
   109	    - `transitive_used_functions_loc`: Lines of code in the used functions of transitive dependencies.
   110	  
   111	
   112	- `rq2a.csv`: Contains the quantitative results for the second research question (RQ2), including all Python projects having vulnerable dependencies. Each row specifies a dependency from a project to a vulnerable dependency.
   113	  - Columns:
   114	    - `project`: GitHub Owner-Repository Name, representing the Python project.
   115	    - `package_name`: Specifies the name of the PyPI package identified as a vulnerable dependency.
   116	    - `dependency_type`: Distinguishes whether the vulnerable package is a direct or transitive dependency of the project.
   117	    - `activation_status`: Indicates the invocation status of the dependency, specifying whether it is a bloated dependency, active, inactive, or undefined.
   118	
   119	- `rq2b.csv`: Contains metrics regarding the usage of inactive (used while the vulnerable method is bloated) and active vulnerable packages within each Python project (RQ2). Each row describes a project’s interaction with a vulnerable dependency and more precisely the extent of bloat and usage in both the files and methods of this dependency.
   120	  - Columns:
   121	    - `project`: GitHub Owner-Repository Name, signifying the particular Python project being analyzed.
   122	    - `package_name`: Specifies the name of the PyPI package identified as a vulnerable dependency.
   123	    - `activation_status`: Indicates the invocation status of the dependency, specifying whether it is active or inactive.
   124	    - `bloated_files`: Quantifies the number of bloated files present in the vulnerable dependency.
   125	    - `used_files`: Enumerates the number of files from the vulnerable dependency that are actually utilized in the project.
   126	    - `bloated_methods`: Enumerates the number of bloated methods present in the vulnerable dependency.
   127	    - `used_methods`: Measures the number of methods from the vulnerable dependency that are actually utilized in the project.
   128	    - `percentage_bloated_methods`: Calculates the percentage of bloated methods within the methods of the vulnerable dependency.
   129	    - `percentage_bloated_files`: Computes the percentage of bloated files within the files of the vulnerable dependency.
   130	
   131	- `qualitative_results.json`: This file contains the results of qualitative analysis conducted for research questions 3 and 4 (RQ3-RQ4) for the 50 selected bloated dependencies. Each record in the file represents a specific project with one or more dependencies that were analyzed. The key of each record is the project name, and its value is a set of JSON objects, where each object represents a dependency in the project. Each dependency object contains the following metadata:
   132	  - `Root Cause`: Describes the root cause of the bloated dependency, as devised from our Root Cause Analysis (RQ3)
   133	  - `PR Status`: Indicates the status of the associated pull request (PR), whether it's merged, open or closed. (Applicable only for dependencies for which we opened PRs)
   134	  - `PR URL`: Provides the URL of the pull request related to the dependency.
   135	  - `Duration`: Represents the duration of the pull request in days.
   136	  - `Created At`: Specifies the date and time when the pull request related to the dependency was opened.
   137	  - `Merged At`: (Optional) Specifies the date and time when the pull request related to the dependency was merged.
   138	  - `Version`: Represents the version of the dependency being removed.
   139	  - `LoC`: Stands for Lines of Code, indicating the number of lines of code of the dependency.
   140	  - `Size`: Specifies the size of the dependency in bytes
   141	  - `Discussion Status`: Indicates the status of any discussions or conversations related to the dependency.
   142	
   143	Bellow is an example of a project entity in the JSON structure:
   144	
   145	```json
   146	  "ewels/MultiQC": {
   147	      "simplejson": {
   148	          "Root Cause": "Built-in or alternate library",
   149	          "PR Status": "Merged",
   150	          "PR URL": "https://github.com/ewels/MultiQC/pull/1973",
   151	          "Duration": 4,
   152	          "Created At": "2023-08-11T00:27:57Z",
   153	          "Merged At": "2023-08-15T21:15:16Z",
   154	          "Version": "3.19.1",
   155	          "LoC": 4500,
   156	          "Size": 515330,
   157	          "Discussion Status": "No Discussion"
   158	      }
   159	  }
   160	```
   161	- `project_dependencies_post_data_collection.json`: This JSON file describes the status of our dataset after the Data Collection phase. Each key represents a GitHub project, and the values represent a list with the PyPI releases of the resolved dependencies. (Its descriptive statistics are described on the third line of Table 1).
   162	```json
   163	[
   164	    {
   165	      "rdiff-backup/rdiff-backup": [
   166	        "PyYAML:6.0"
   167	      ]
   168	    },
   169	    {
   170	      "jopohl/urh": [
   171	        "psutil:5.9.5",
   172	        "numpy:1.25.0",
   173	        "PyQt5-sip:12.12.1",
   174	        "PyQt5:5.15.9",
   175	        "Cython:0.29.36",
   176	        "PyQt5-Qt5:5.15.2"
   177	      ]
   178	    }
   179	  // More projects...
   180	]
   181	```
   182	- `project_dependencies_final.json`: This JSON file describes the status of our dataset after the Data Analysis phase. It is a subset of the `project_dependencies_post_data_collection.json` file and its descriptive statistics are described on the third line of Table 1 of the paper.
   183	- `security/`: This directory stores the data generated when running our methodology for answering RQ2 (detailed in the second paragraph of Section 2.4 of our paper)
   184	  - `pypi_vulnerabilities.csv`:  This file contains the set of PyPI vulnerabilities extracted from the GitHub Advisory Database.
   185	  - Columns:
   186	    - `Identifier`: GitHub Owner-Repository Name, signifying the particular Python project being analyzed.
   187	    - `Package`: Specifies the name of the affected PyPI package
   188	    - `VersionConstraint`: Describes the package versions affected by this vulnerability, in the format of comma-separated version constraints (e.g. ">= 4.0,< 4.0.7")
   189	  - `vulnerable_dependencies.json`: This JSON file serves as a record of vulnerable releases acting as dependencies in our dataset. Each record consists of a key representing a PyPI release and a list of affected Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVEs). For example:
